                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='7331' id='12' type-v2='text' w='13429' x='86000' y='667'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                    <format attr='background-color' value='#272d36' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='12084' id='80' type-v2='text' w='92431' x='3781' y='10665'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4629ff' fontsize='14'>Introduction</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Welcome to the Job Catalog Quality Dashboard. This dashboard helps you monitor and improve the quality of job profile data within our organization. The dashboard consists of three key sections each providing different insights into the job catalog data. This instruction page is meant to ensure you understand the components of the dashboard, the methodology behind the data model, and how to effectively use the dashboard to foster continuous improvement in our job catalog quality.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#e15759' fontsize='11'>Note: Achieving 100% good quality is not the goal, as our model is a quantitative analysis tool. It is designed to guide improvements rather than prescribe perfection.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='58502' id='78' type-v2='text' w='46216' x='3781' y='25415'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4629ff' fontsize='14'>Sections Overview</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Main KPIs:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Good Quality Job Profiles %: </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Displays the percentage of job profiles that are considered to be of good quality based on our data model.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Headcount by Quality:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Shows the total number of job profiles considered as good quality and low quality which are currently under assessment.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Under Assessment Job Profiles %:</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Indicates the percentage of job profiles considered to be of low quality which are currently under assessment.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Monthly - Trended Job Profile Quality:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>This section visualizes the progress of job profile quality over time. The data is displayed on a monthly basis, allowing you to observe trends and improvements over specific periods.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Job Profile Quality per Dimension:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>This section provides a detailed comparison of good quality and under-assessment cases across different dimensions such as Brand, Country, Company, Job Family, and Job Family Group. This helps in identifying specific areas that might need more attention or have shown significant improvement.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4629ff' fontsize='14'>How to Use the Dashboard</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Navigate the Sections:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Start by reviewing the Main KPIs to get a high-level overview of job catalog quality.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Move to the Trend Over Time section to understand how the quality has evolved monthly.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Dive into the Detailed View to perform a more granular analysis based on different dimensions.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Identify Patterns and Trends:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Use the Trend Over Time section to spot significant changes or trends in job profile quality.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>In the Detailed View, filter and compare different dimensions to pinpoint specific areas requiring attention.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Generate Insights and Actions:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Leverage the insights gained from the dashboard to drive targeted actions aimed at improving data quality.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Focus on areas with lower quality scores or higher under-assessment cases to prioritize improvements.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='33208' id='79' type-v2='text' w='46215' x='49997' y='25415'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#4629ff' fontsize='14'>Data Model</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Our data model for detecting low quality data points is based on three foundational pillars:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>String Matching:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>This technique identifies good quality cases by detecting common words between Job Profile and Business Title. It is a straightforward method that looks for direct matches or overlaps in terminology.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Data Science Model:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Utilizing Natural Language Processing (NLP), this model identifies cases where Job Profile and Business Title are semantically similar, even if there are no common words. This allows for detection of contextual similarities, improving the robustness of our quality assessment.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#72b966' fontsize='10'>Word Mapping:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Enhanced by a combination of human expertise and machine learning observations, this approach instructs common accurate or inaccurate pairings based on historical data and expert inputs. It helps in refining the model&apos;s accuracy over time.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone fixed-size='144' h='12647' id='87' is-fixed='true' is-scaled='1' param='Image/1.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='46215' x='49997' y='58623'>
